Limit use of the body armor slot, then.  DSM can cover a broad range of
intrinsics, and body armor is the most out of character for what I think
you're trying to do.

If you're looking at Conan, he tanked up rather nicely in the books
(including REH's); his primary armor limitations were based on
circumstnace more than philosophy.  Much of the time he simply had no
access to it, or it had been broken, or the situation called for a light
load (breaking into the Elephant's Tower, for example), or similar.

Limiting the barbarian to offcast pieces of armor -- gloves, helmets,
boots especially -- is within the trope I think you're looking for.

